h2 Frequently Asked Questions

.content
  h3 Browser Compatibility Issues

  h4 "Connection is not private" message in Safari
  p Some transcribers may encounter a "Connection is not private" warning message when trying to access FromThePage in Safari. This is commonly caused by antivirus software, particularly Avast, interfering with SSL connections.

  p 
    strong Solution:
  ul
    li If you are using Avast antivirus, you can resolve this by excluding FromThePage from Avast's web scanning:
      ol
        li Open Avast Antivirus
        li Go to Settings → General → Exceptions
        li Add <code>*.fromthepage.com</code> to the website exceptions
        li Restart your browser and try accessing FromThePage again
    li Alternatively, you can temporarily disable Avast's HTTPS scanning feature while using FromThePage
    li If the issue persists, try accessing FromThePage using a different browser such as Chrome or Firefox

  p 
    | For more detailed instructions on configuring Avast exclusions, please see the 
    = link_to "official Avast support guide", "https://support.avast.com/en-ww/article/Antivirus-scan-exclusions", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener"
    | .

  p 
    | Learn more about this issue in this 
    = link_to "technical article", "https://itnerd.blog/2015/05/21/avast-responds-to-my-post-about-their-anti-virus-product/", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener"
    | .

.content  
  h3 General Questions

  h4 What is FromThePage?
  p FromThePage is a collaborative transcription platform that allows institutions and volunteers to work together to transcribe historical documents and make them searchable and accessible online.

  h4 How do I get started transcribing?
  p Simply browse our public collections, find a document that interests you, and click "Transcribe" to begin. No account registration is required for guest transcription, though creating an account allows you to track your contributions.

  h4 What browsers work best with FromThePage?
  p FromThePage works with all modern browsers including Chrome, Firefox, Safari, and Edge. For the best experience, we recommend using the latest version of your preferred browser.

